/*  Reversible logic — gates that throw nothing away, and a two-bit adder built from them.

    An ordinary AND gate takes two wires in and gives one out, so the inputs cannot be
    recovered afterwards: the gate destroys information. A REVERSIBLE gate has as many
    wires out as in and merely permutes them, so every state has exactly one predecessor.
    Three of them are enough to build anything — NOT, controlled-NOT, and the
    doubly-controlled NOT that Toffoli showed is universal on its own.

    ★★ Every gate here is its OWN inverse, so the undoing circuit is not a second circuit.
    It is this one, walked backwards. That is what the program checks: drive the adder
    forwards, drive the same gates in the opposite order, and the register must be the one
    it started with, bit for bit.

    ⚠ Reversibility is not free. The adder answers in three wires and leaves two more
    holding values nobody asked for. They cannot be dropped — dropping them is precisely
    the information loss the gates exist to avoid — and carrying them is what makes the
    run backwards possible at all.
*/

// The register is a `bits` value and a wire is one of its digits, counted from the LEFT as
// printed: wire 1 of `0b10000000` is the one that is set. The width is read off the value
// rather than fixed, so the same three gates drive a register of any size.
//
//     wire     1    2    3    4    5    6    7    8
//              a0   a1   b0   b1   c0   c1   c2   ·
//
// `a` and `b` are the two-bit numbers being added, low bit first. `c0`, `c1` and `c2` start
// at zero and end holding the answer — c0 the low bit of the sum, c1 the high one, c2 the
// carry out. Wire 8 is never touched.

Define object flip with (the number target).
Define object flip-if with (the number control, the number target).
Define object flip-if-both with (the number left-control, the number right-control, the number target).

Bind bits to wire-mask, given (the bits register, the number wire):
    Define span as the width of register.
    Return 0b1 shifted left by (span - wire).
Done.

Bind fact to wire-set, given (the bits register, the number wire):
    Return (register and cast wire-mask on (register, wire)) is not 0b0.
Done.

// The register is always the LEFT operand, which is what keeps the result eight digits
// wide: a mask built by shifting `0b1` carries only the width it grew into.
Bind bits to flip-wire, given (the bits register, the number wire):
    Return register xor cast wire-mask on (register, wire).
Done.

Bind number to wire-value, given (the bits register, the number wire):
    If cast wire-set on (register, wire), return 1.
    Return 0.
Done.

// A closed union of three, so the Judge needs no Otherwise — the checker can see every
// gate is covered, and adding a fourth kind would make this arm list fail to compile
// rather than silently ignore it.
Bind bits to apply, given (the (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both) gate, the bits register):
    Judge gate, where it is:
        A flip, return cast flip-wire on (register, the target of it).
        A flip-if:
            If cast wire-set on (register, the control of it),
                return cast flip-wire on (register, the target of it).
            Return register.
        Done.
        A flip-if-both:
            Define left-on as cast wire-set on (register, the left-control of it).
            Define right-on as cast wire-set on (register, the right-control of it).
            If left-on and right-on, return cast flip-wire on (register, the target of it).
            Return register.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.

// ⚠ There is no standalone reversal for a series. `in reverse` only modifies `sorted`, and
// sorting a circuit would destroy the very thing that makes it a circuit — its order. So the
// undoing pass is built by hand, prepending each gate as it goes.
Bind catalogue of (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both) to undoing, given (the catalogue of (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both) circuit):
    Define backwards as a catalogue of (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both).
    For each gate in circuit, repeat:
        Insert gate into the start of backwards.
    Done.
    Return backwards.
Done.

Bind bits to drive, given (the catalogue of (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both) circuit, the bits register):
    Define current as register.
    For each gate in circuit, repeat:
        The current becomes cast apply on (gate, current).
    Done.
    Return current.
Done.

/*  One reversible full adder, four gates:

        Toffoli(left, right -> c-out)   carry-out ^= left and right
        CNOT(left -> right)             right becomes left xor right
        Toffoli(right, c-in -> c-out)   carry-out ^= (left xor right) and carry-in
        CNOT(right -> carry-in)         carry-in becomes left xor right xor carry-in — the sum

    ★ The carry-in wire ends up holding the SUM, and the carry-out wire holds the carry.
    That is what lets stages chain without any extra wires: the carry-out of one stage is
    the carry-in of the next, so a wire is a carry on the way in and a sum bit on the way
    out. The left wire survives untouched; the right one is left holding `left xor right`,
    and that is the garbage. */
Bind catalogue of (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both) to full-adder, given (the number left-wire, the number right-wire, the number carry-in, the number carry-out):
    Return a catalogue of (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both) with (
        a new flip-if-both { the left-control left-wire, the right-control right-wire, the target carry-out },
        a new flip-if { the control left-wire, the target right-wire },
        a new flip-if-both { the left-control right-wire, the right-control carry-in, the target carry-out },
        a new flip-if { the control right-wire, the target carry-in }).
Done.

Bind catalogue of (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both) to two-bit-adder:
    Define circuit as a catalogue of (flip or flip-if or flip-if-both).
    For each gate in cast full-adder on (1, 3, 5, 6), repeat: Insert gate into circuit. Done.
    For each gate in cast full-adder on (2, 4, 6, 7), repeat: Insert gate into circuit. Done.
    Return circuit.
Done.

// Wires 1 and 2 carry `a`, wires 3 and 4 carry `b`, low bit first.
Bind bits to load, given (the number first-number, the number second-number):
    Define register as 0b00000000.
    If first-number % 2 is 1, register becomes cast flip-wire on (register, 1).
    If first-number is 2 or first-number is 3, register becomes cast flip-wire on (register, 2).
    If second-number % 2 is 1, register becomes cast flip-wire on (register, 3).
    If second-number is 2 or second-number is 3, register becomes cast flip-wire on (register, 4).
    Return register.
Done.

Pull a rabbit.
    Define circuit as cast two-bit-adder.
    Define backwards as cast undoing on (circuit).

    State "  a  b   sum  undone".
    For each first-number in range 0 to 3, repeat:
        For each second-number in range 0 to 3, repeat:
            Define loaded as cast load on (first-number, second-number).
            Define finished as cast drive on (circuit, loaded).

            Define low as cast wire-value on (finished, 5).
            Define high as cast wire-value on (finished, 6).
            Define carry as cast wire-value on (finished, 7).
            Define total as low + (high * 2) + (carry * 4).

            Define restored as cast drive on (backwards, finished).
            Define undone as "no".
            If restored is loaded, undone becomes "yes".

            State "  {first-number converted to text}  {second-number converted to text}     {total converted to text}  {undone}".
        Done.
    Done.

    // The same run, wire by wire. Wires 3 and 4 come back holding `a0 xor b0` and
    // `a1 xor b1` — nobody asked for either, and the circuit cannot be undone without them.
    Define loaded as cast load on (2, 3).
    Define finished as cast drive on (circuit, loaded).
    State "".
    State "2 + 3, wire by wire".
    State "  before    {loaded converted to text}".
    State "  after     {finished converted to text}".
    State "  sum       {cast wire-value on (finished, 5) converted to text} then {cast wire-value on (finished, 6) converted to text}, carry {cast wire-value on (finished, 7) converted to text}".
    State "  garbage   wire 3 is {cast wire-value on (finished, 3) converted to text}, wire 4 is {cast wire-value on (finished, 4) converted to text}".
    State "  reversed  {cast drive on (backwards, finished) converted to text}".
Done.
